 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	## E46 Areas that hold data: the build says which country, province and basin each dataset sits in — CHARTERED 25 Nov 2026 (Kernel; strategy at lane open; one Codex round)
     2	
     3	Authority: family `MAP-AS-A-SHOP-family.md` (R-S3, R-S4, R-S5, R-S8); OSD-D27, OSD-D28; E03 and E29
     4	(committed outlines), E32 (build shape, tiles), E36 (first-load budget). Evidence:
     5	`global-layers.md` and `build_areas.py` beside the prototype (the prototype counts one point per
     6	dataset and leaves national registers out; this charter replaces that rule with the decided one).
     7	
     8	**Outcome.** After `osd build`, every record in `records.json` says which areas it sits in, per
     9	kind, and the catalogue holds, per kind, exactly the areas that hold at least one dataset, with a
    10	name, a label point and the dataset ids. The shop (E48) draws and filters from these files and
    11	computes nothing itself.
    12	
    13	**Context today (verified on `origin/main` `fd69de4`, 25 Nov).**
    14	
    15	- `src/osd/build.py` `build()` joins records with verification, collects outline features
    16	  (169,295 features: 166,412 well points, the rest survey polygons and lines) and writes
    17	  `records.json`, `outlines.geojson`, well grids and `outlines.pmtiles` (tippecanoe).
    18	- `schema/record.schema.json` is record/5: `region.country` (ISO alpha-2), `region.basin` (free
    19	  text), `region.bbox`. 192 of 236 records carry a bbox. Nothing says a dataset is country-wide; the
    20	  prototype guesses it from the ratio of the box to the country's box.
    21	- `src/osd/outlines/geometry.py` has simplification and ring helpers; there is no point-in-polygon
    22	  and no area data in the repository.
    23	- Network is allowed only in the commands AGENTS.md names; the build is offline.
    24	
    25	**The design the charter fixes.**
    26	
    27	1. *Area files are committed inputs, like outlines.* `areas/<kind>.geojson` for `country`,
    28	   `province`, `basin`, each validated by a new `schema/area.schema.json` (area/1): a
    29	   FeatureCollection whose top level carries `kind`, `source` (`name`, `url`, `licence`, `credit`,
    30	   `edition`, `retrieved`, `sha256` of the publisher's file) and whose features carry `area_id`
    31	   (stable, from the source's own code: ISO alpha-2, `iso_3166_2` or `adm1_code`, the USGS province
    32	   code), `name`, and for provinces `country`. Geometry is simplified once, at preparation, to what
    33	   zoom 8 can show; the three files together stay under 25 MB in git. Licence areas (E51) use the
    34	   same schema with `kind: licence`, so E51 adds files, not a contract.
    35	2. *Preparation is a maintainer command, not the build.* `osd areas prepare <kind> <file>` reads a
    36	   publisher file already on the machine (Natural Earth 50m countries, Natural Earth 10m admin-1,
    37	   USGS WEP_PRVG; shapefile or GeoJSON, read as data, never executed), simplifies, and writes the
    38	   committed area file with the source block. It reaches no network; AGENTS.md's network line is
    39	   unchanged. The publisher files themselves are not committed; `areas/SOURCES.md` records where
    40	   each was taken from, its digest and its terms sentence, quoted.
    41	3. *record/6: a dataset can say it is country-wide.* Optional `region.national: true`: the
    42	   publisher presents the dataset as covering the country named in `region.country` (a national
    43	   register, a national survey). A publisher fact; E52 fills it. record/5 files still validate.
    44	4. *The count (R-S3), in `osd build`, module `src/osd/areas.py`.* For each record, its positions
    45	   are: every committed outline feature of the record (a well point as itself; a polygon or line by
    46	   its vertices and one interior point); when it has none, the middle of `region.bbox`; when it
    47	   has neither, no position. A record sits in an area when at least one position lies inside it.
    48	   A record with `region.national` sits in its country and, by this rule alone, in no province or
    49	   basin unless it has outline positions (a national register with committed wells does light the
    50	   basins its wells are in: that is the point of the ruling). A record without `national` and
    51	   without positions but with `region.country` counts for the country.
    52	   Containment is exact on the committed (simplified) geometry, with a bounding-box index so the
    53	   166,412 points cost seconds, and the per-register result is cached under `build/` keyed by the
    54	   digests of the outline and area files so `make check` stays inside its two minutes.
    55	5. *What the build writes.* `records.json`: each record gains `areas: {country: [...], province:
    56	   [...], basin: [...]}` (area ids, sorted; a kind absent when empty). `build/catalog/areas.json`
    57	   (areas/1 index): per kind the `source` block and the list of areas that hold a dataset:
    58	   `area_id`, `name`, `label` ([lon, lat] inside the largest part), `bbox`, `n`, `ids`.
    59	   Geometry of those areas only goes to tiles: one layer per kind (`areas_country`,
    60	   `areas_province`, `areas_basin`) in a separate `areas.pmtiles`, feature id = a stable integer,
    61	   properties `area_id`, `name`, `n` only; and `areas-<kind>.geojson` beside it as the fallback for
    62	   a server without byte ranges and for the offline tests. An area that holds nothing is in neither.
    63	6. *Slices.* Slice 0 is the contract and lands first, alone: area/1 and record/6 schemas with their
    64	   old-file tests, `osd validate` reading `areas/`, a fixture set under `tests/fixtures/areas/`
    65	   (three small countries, four provinces, three basins, six records: a register with wells across
    66	   two basins, a survey polygon across a border, a bbox-only dataset, a `national` one, one with
    67	   nothing, one whose bbox middle falls in the sea), the expected `areas.json` for it committed as
    68	   the golden file, and `build()` writing `areas.json` and `records[].areas` from whatever is in
    69	   `areas/` (nothing yet: empty lists, valid files). Slice 1 commits the three real area files and
    70	   `SOURCES.md`, the tiles, the cache, and the numbers.
    71	
    72	**Acceptance.**
    73	
    74	1. Slice 0: `schema/area.schema.json` exists with `$id` …/area/1; record schema `$id` is
    75	   …/record/6; every record/5 file on main validates against record/6 (test kept); a test shows a
    76	   record/5 fixture file still valid and `region.national: "yes"` invalid.
    77	2. Slice 0: the fixture build's `areas.json` equals the golden file byte for byte; each of the six
    78	   fixture records has the `areas` the charter's rule gives, asserted one by one with the reason
    79	   in the test name.
    80	3. Slice 0: with an empty `areas/`, `osd build` writes a valid `areas.json` with empty lists and
    81	   no `areas` key on records, and the live site's tests pass unchanged.
    82	4. Slice 1: `areas/country.geojson`, `province.geojson`, `basin.geojson` validate, total under
    83	   25 MB; `areas/SOURCES.md` quotes each terms sentence and digest; the PR states how many areas of
    84	   each kind hold a dataset and how many datasets are placed per kind, beside the prototype's
    85	   (933 named basins, 4,590 provinces, 121 datasets with a place).
    86	5. Slice 1: no area with `n = 0` in `areas.json`, the tiles or the fallback files (test over the
    87	   real build); every `ids` entry is a record id; every record's `areas` agrees with the index in
    88	   both directions.
    89	6. Slice 1: the Sodir register lights more than one basin and exactly one country; a record with
    90	   `national` and no outline lights its country and no basin (tests on the real catalogue, written
    91	   so that E52's edits do not break them).
    92	7. Guards, one mutation each shown to fail: a point on the far side of a hole is outside; a
    93	   polygon crossing the antimeridian is handled as the committed outlines handle it; the bbox middle
    94	   is used only when no outline exists; an area file whose `source.licence` is empty is refused by
    95	   `osd validate`.
    96	8. `make check` on CI stays under 120 s (number in the PR); first load of the live page is
    97	   unchanged (it requests none of the new files).
    98	
    99	**Out of scope.** Drawing anything (E48); licence areas (E51); filling `national` (E52); renaming
   100	or removing `region.basin`; STAC exposure of areas.
   101	
   102	**Stop rules.** If exact containment for the five large registers cannot be cached to keep
   103	`make check` under 120 s, stop and write the measured times to the inbox with the default
   104	"count the large registers from their well-grid cells at z6 and say so in `areas.json`".
   105	If the three area files cannot be brought under 25 MB at a tolerance that still reads at zoom 8,
   106	stop with the sizes; do not raise the budget alone.
   107	
