     1	# The map as a shop (E46–E53): one page where a person finds, picks and takes open subsurface data
     2	
     3	Authority: owner, 25 Nov 2026. The design was drawn in rounds on Paper (file "OpenSubsurfaceData",
     4	page "Where we want to be: the map as a shop", boards Shop 01–06; page "Open questions", boards
     5	Open 01 and 02, both decided) and accepted with "go with your recommendations" / "go with all your
     6	recommendations" / "go with your advice". The owner's rulings are OSD-D26 to OSD-D31. The working
     7	prototype and the three studies are at `~/.local/share/osd-program/prototype-2026-11-25/` on the
     8	controller (`index.html`, `build_areas.py`, `speed-practices.md`, `global-layers.md`,
     9	`block-layers.md`; `b6.py` holds the text of every board). The prototype is evidence of the design,
    10	not source: every lane rebuilds in this repository's structure and copies nothing in.
    11	
    12	Builds on E05 (map, hash state, Playwright site test), E06 (select, manifest/4, `osd get`), E15 and
    13	E36 (tiles, well grids, first load under 1 MB), E21 and E27 (when, why), E32 (build shape), E43
    14	(starter cards), E07 (mirror).
    15	
    16	**Review.** Kernel charters E46, E49 and E51 each get one Codex round (OSD-D8); dispositions are
    17	recorded under each charter. E47, E48, E50, E53 (Surface) and E52 (Records) get none.
    18	
    19	**Why this family exists.** Today the site is a map with a filter panel, a detail panel and three
    20	side pages (How, Status, Starter projects). A person who arrives cannot see at a glance what exists
    21	where they are looking, the map draws a rectangle for a dataset that covers a country, and taking
    22	data means a manifest and a command line. The agreed design turns the one page into a shop: look at
    23	a place, see the list for that place, add to a bag, leave with the files, a Python file, or (later)
    24	an Ophiolite project.
    25	
    26	**The page.**
    27	
    28	```text
    29	┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
    30	│ Open Subsurface Data   [ search …………………………… ]  [Filters]            [Bag · 3] │
    31	├───────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
    32	│ 101 datasets in this view │                                                  │
    33	│ ⊕ NLOG            ⤓       │                     the map                      │
    34	│ ✓ Volve           ⤓       │   blue sea, green and sand land; no legend       │
    35	│ ⊕ UKCS wells      ✉       │   an area is drawn only when a dataset sits in it│
    36	│ …  (follows the map)      │                                                  │
    37	│                           │  [Countries|Provinces|Basins]  [Names]  [Flat|Globe] │
    38	└───────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
    39	 ⊕ round green plus, ✓ when in the bag; the small icon says how the dataset is obtained
    40	 Bag (right): Download the files · Get a Python file · (Open in Ophiolite: not shipped, R-S6)
    41	```
    42	
    43	**The journey (the contract every slice lights a part of).** `tests/site/shop.test.mjs` holds these
    44	steps under these names from E47 on; a step no merged slice lights yet is a `test.todo` naming its
    45	epic. E53 may replace the front page only when none is left.
    46	
    47	| Step | A person… | Lit by |
    48	|---|---|---|
    49	| J1 | opens the page and within the budget sees the search bar, a list and the map; no legend, no side pages needed | E47 |
    50	| J2 | pans or zooms and the list is exactly the datasets of the map window, each once, with its count | E47 |
    51	| J3 | types in the search bar and the list and the map narrow | E47 |
    52	| J4 | opens Filters (one button), sets kind, level, years, access, starter; closes it; the button shows how many are set | E47 |
    53	| J5 | presses the green plus on a row: it becomes a tick, the bag count goes up; nothing on the map changes colour | E47 |
    54	| J6 | reads from the row's small icon how the dataset is obtained (download, sign-in, API, on request, purchase) | E47 |
    55	| J7 | opens a row and reads what E21, E27 and E43 said: when, why at this level, starter project | E47 |
    56	| J8 | switches Countries / Provinces / Basins: only areas holding a dataset are drawn; a click on one filters the list to it; a second click or the chip's cross clears it | E48 (data E46) |
    57	| J9 | turns Names on and off: one name per drawn area | E48 |
    58	| J10 | switches Flat / Globe: same data, same clicks | E48 |
    59	| J11 | opens the bag and downloads: a manifest/4 for `osd get`, and direct links for files the catalogue holds | E47 |
    60	| J12 | takes "Get a Python file": a `.py` that runs as written against the catalogue | E49 |
    61	| J13 | switches to Licences where a regulator is read: licences holding a dataset are drawn, the row names the block | E51 |
    62	| J14 | shares the address: a second browser shows the same window, filters, outline kind, area and bag | E47, E48 |
    63	| J15 | does J1, J2, J5 and J11 on a phone-width screen | E47 |
    64	
    65	**Family rules.**
    66	
    67	- **R-S1 The live site stays usable at every merge.** The shop lives at `site/shop.html` (with
    68	  `site/shop.js`, `site/shop.css`) until E53. `site/index.html` and `site/app.js` are not edited
    69	  by this family before E53 except for a defect. No link to the shop from the live pages before E53.
    70	- **R-S2 Show the thing itself.** No legend on the map. No colour on the map for what is in the
    71	  bag. No row of three decorative cards anywhere (owner, 24 Nov). Credits required by a source go
    72	  in the map's attribution line, nowhere else.
    73	- **R-S3 An area is drawn only when a dataset sits in it, and the build decides.** "Sits in it" is
    74	  counted by `osd build` from real well positions and survey outlines (the committed outlines);
    75	  a dataset without positions uses the middle of its box; a country-wide dataset counts for its
    76	  country only. The browser never computes containment. Every drawn area is clickable and filters
    77	  the list. One name per area.
    78	- **R-S4 One exclusive switch.** Countries / Provinces / Basins, later Licences. Never two kinds at
    79	  once.
    80	- **R-S5 Sources are named with their terms.** Countries and provinces: Natural Earth (public
    81	  domain). Basins: USGS "Geologic Provinces of the World" (WEP_PRVG; use constraints none; credit
    82	  "U.S. Geological Survey"). Licences: per country from the regulator, each licence text read and
    83	  its credit line recorded before the first byte is committed (E51). A source without read terms
    84	  is not drawn.
    85	- **R-S6 No "Open in Ophiolite" button** until the whole path works: Ophiolite has no public
    86	  sign-up; its supervisor sends the landing address shape. Not a hidden button, not a disabled
    87	  one: absent. The row mark for a built sample project waits with it.
    88	- **R-S7 Speed is an acceptance line, not a hope.** Target (owner): map usable within 2 s of
    89	  opening, 60 pictures a second while dragging and zooming, no download for an area visited in the
    90	  same visit, no download of our files for a return visit. The list is filtered from the page's own
    91	  records by the map window, never from tile queries. First-load budget stays under 1 MB from the
    92	  site (E36). The four owed measurements are E50's acceptance with numbers in the PR.
    93	- **R-S8 The house rules hold.** One HTML, one JS, one CSS per page, no build step, no framework.
    94	  Schemas are contracts. Records state publisher facts. `make check` stays offline and under two
    95	  minutes; no station is added to it.
    96	- **R-S9 Look.** Ophiolite house look: Merriweather titles, Roboto text, night blue `#101824`,
    97	  amber `#e0912f` for the one action in the bag. Base map in familiar colours (blue sea, green and
    98	  sand land). Fonts are loaded so that text is readable before they arrive.
    99	
   100	**Epics and order.**
   101	
   102	```text
   103	E46 s0 contract ──▶ E46 s1 countries, provinces, basins ──▶ E48 outlines, names, globe ──▶ E53 front page
   104	        │                                                        ▲
   105	        ├──▶ E52 country-wide datasets (records)                 │
   106	        └──▶ E51 s1.. licences (UK, NO, US)  ◀── E51 s0 terms    │
   107	E47 the one-page shop ───────────────────────────────────────────┤
   108	E49 the Python file (kernel) ──▶ its button in the bag (after E47)│
   109	E50 speed and the four measurements (after E47, again after E48) ─┘
   110	```
   111	
   112	Open at once, files disjoint: E46, E47, E49, E51 slice 0. After E46 slice 0: E52. After E46 slice 1
   113	and E47: E48. After E47: E50. After E48 and E46: E51 slices 1–3. Last: E53.
   114	
   115	| Epic | Class | Outcome |
   116	|---|---|---|
   117	| E46 Areas that hold data | Kernel | The build says which country, province and basin each dataset sits in, and writes only the areas that hold one |
   118	| E47 The one-page shop | Surface | Search, a list that follows the map, Filters behind one button, the plus, the bag |
   119	| E48 Outlines, names and the globe | Surface | One switch for the outline kind, clickable areas, names, Flat and Globe |
   120	| E49 The Python file | Kernel | `import osd; osd.get("opm/norne")` and the file the bag writes |
   121	| E50 Speed, measured | Surface (with build) | The Shop 06 practices in place and the four measurements with numbers |
   122	| E51 Licences per country | Kernel + Records | Licences from the UK, Norway and the United States as a fourth outline kind, as fresh as the regulator |
   123	| E52 Country-wide datasets say so | Records | Every national register carries the publisher's statement that it covers the country |
   124	| E53 The shop becomes the front page | Surface | opensubsurfacedata.org opens on the shop; How, Status and Starter projects are folded in |
   125	
   126	**Not in this family.** Mirror growth for small allowed datasets (inbox item of 25 Nov, a later
   127	charter); the Ophiolite landing and the sample-project tree (Ophiolite E211); Canada and Australia
   128	licences (after their terms are read, a follow-on to E51); any account, payment or server.
