     1	"""Build the published catalogue from records, outlines and verification records.
     2	
     3	Outputs (build/catalog/):
     4	  records.json    every record, joined with its latest verification level, the date it was
     5	                   established, `stale` when that date is over 30 days old (or absent) and
     6	                   `blocked_since` while the origin refuses this runner (OSD-D9); `reasons`, by record
     7	                   id, why the record is at its level in the verifier's words ("never verified" when
     8	                   it never was), the very string `osd status` prints (osd.reasons, E27), kept beside
     9	                   the records array so records_digest and the manifests that pin it are unchanged;
    10	                   and `catalog`,
    11	                   the snapshot identity (E09): source_commit, verification_commit, built_at and
    12	                   records_digest, the sha256 of the records array as canonical JSON (keys sorted,
    13	                   separators "," ":", UTF-8), which manifest/3 and fidelity/1 carry back
    14	  outlines.geojson one FeatureCollection, every feature joined with record title, kinds,
    15	                   licence and level so the map needs no second lookup
    16	  stac/            the static STAC catalogue (src/osd/stac.py)
    17	  collections.json {"collections": [...]}, the same STAC Collections in one file
    18	  outlines.pmtiles the same features as vector tiles, z0-12, when tippecanoe is installed (E15);
    19	                   wellbore points from CLUSTER_BELOW_ZOOM up only (E36)
    20	  wells-z<z>.json  for z below CLUSTER_BELOW_ZOOM, the wellbore points counted on a grid (E36): what
    21	                   the map clusters there, so the world view does not load every well
    22	  mirror.json     {"copies": [...]}, the public index of what the mirror holds, regenerated from the
    23	                   custody documents in <mirror_dir>/custody/ (E07, custody/1 and /2); STAC assets gain
    24	                   the alternates
    25	  starters.json   {"starters": [...]}, every published starter pack whole (E40): each pack document that
    26	                   passes every rule of osd.starters with its evidence here, is not `unpublished`, plus
    27	                   `record` (the record's title and level) and each artefact's `href` from its custody
    28	                   document; the record in records.json lists the pack ids in `starters` (only records
    29	                   with a pack carry the key). A refused or unchecked pack is printed, never published
    30	  starters/       each published pack document and its fidelity record, byte for byte (the pack
    31	                   manifest's two documents, osd manifest --starter)
    32	"""
    33	
    34	from __future__ import annotations
    35	
    36	import hashlib
    37	import json
    38	import os
    39	import re
    40	import shutil
    41	import subprocess
    42	from datetime import UTC, datetime
    43	from pathlib import Path
    44	
    45	from . import __version__, mirror, paths, stac, starters
    46	from .reasons import reason
