docs/program/DECISIONS.md:19:| OSD-D12 | Derived outlines are committed | `outlines/*.geojson` are committed although derived, because their inputs are remote and mutable: a rerun is a reviewable diff, and the file is the contract E04/E05 read. Every derived feature carries the input identity (address and sha256 of the bytes used). This is the one recorded exception to ENGINEERING rule R7 | DEFAULT 23 Oct (E03 review) |
docs/program/DECISIONS.md:20:| OSD-D13 | Outline licence | Outlines derived from a publisher's data carry that publisher's licence, not CC0: each feature gets `licence` from its record, and `records/LICENSE` dedicates only the hand-written records and catalogue metadata | DEFAULT 23 Oct (E03 review) |
docs/program/DECISIONS.md:21:| OSD-D14 | STAC items and time | STAC Items need a datetime or a bounded interval. Collections are always emitted; Items only for features whose record declares a `period` (publisher-stated acquisition or release interval) or whose feature carries a publisher date. The GeoJSON stays the per-feature address for everything else | DEFAULT 23 Oct (E04 review) |
docs/program/DECISIONS.md:23:| OSD-D16 | Size of derived outlines | Survey polygons derived from bin grids are simplified in the extractor with a tolerance named per record in `src/osd/outlines/rules.yaml` (default 50 m, below the bin size the staircase encodes) and `simplified_m` is recorded on each feature; wellbore points stay exact; target under 2 MB per outline file, except register outlines (Sodir, NLOG: thousands of wellbores and hundreds of surveys), which may reach 8 MB until a tiling lane produces PMTiles; input identity is carried once per file in the collection's `inputs` member and features name their input; polygon rings with area below tolerance² are dropped and counted; 2D survey polygons (buffered line networks) are written as exteriors only and polygon coordinates are rounded to 5 decimals (E03-3, Sodir 10 MB otherwise). Amended 23 Oct on E03-2 (Sodir 14 MB after simplification, mostly repeated identity). Amended 24 Oct on E32 (supervisor): since E15 the site reads PMTiles, not outline files, so a register outline file of a layer above 20,000 features may reach 25 MB (North Dakota 17.5 MB, Utah 13.6, BCER 13.3, SGC 9.0); the staged site stays under 500 MB (E32 measured 485.6 MB). The simplified file is the committed contract (OSD-D12). Tiling at scale stays the PMTiles path the E05 page already loads | DEFAULT 23 Oct (E03 inbox; NLOG and Sodir outlines were 12 MB each unsimplified) |
docs/program/DECISIONS.md:37:| OSD-D34 | Work in progress for this family | R1 (two coding lanes plus one records lane) is a floor, not a cap, for E46–E53: as many Opus lanes side by side as have disjoint claimed paths; the claims board keeps them apart; the controller's disk is checked before a lane is added | DECIDED by the owner 25 Nov 2026 ("open as many agents as you need … so that we don't wait for features too long") |
