     1	## E51 Licences per country: the United Kingdom, Norway and the United States as a fourth outline kind, as fresh as the regulator — CHARTERED 25 Nov 2026 (Kernel + Records; strategy at lane open; one Codex round)
     2	
     3	Authority: family `MAP-AS-A-SHOP-family.md` (journey J13; R-S3, R-S5); OSD-D29; board Open 02
     4	(`b6.py`); `block-layers.md` beside the prototype (service addresses, counts and what was and was
     5	not verified on 25 Nov 2026). E29, E35, E38 (ArcGIS and WFS readers), H2 (verify in shards), E46.
     6	
     7	**The owner's ruling.** No free world layer exists, so licences are read per country from the
     8	regulator, on a schedule. Order: United Kingdom, Norway, United States; then Canada and Australia
     9	once their terms are read. Draw licences (what a company holds), not grid blocks; draw only those
    10	that hold a dataset; name the block in the dataset row.
    11	
    12	**Outcome.** On the shop, Licences is a fourth choice of the outline switch in the countries that
    13	are read. A licence is drawn when a real well or survey outline of a dataset lies in it; a click
    14	filters the list to those datasets; an opened dataset row says which block or licence its wells
    15	are in. The date the regulator was last read is shown in the attribution line. A regulator that
    16	does not answer leaves the last good copy in place and says so.
    17	
    18	**Context today.** `src/osd/verifier/` reads ArcGIS FeatureServer layers whole (E35) and WFS 2.0.0
    19	GeoJSON (E38), with robots (H3) and shards (H2). `verify.yml` runs on dispatch only; PROGRAM rule
    20	R6 says no timers. E46 defines area/1 and the count for any `kind`. From `block-layers.md`:
    21	
    22	| Country | Service (25 Nov) | Layer to draw | Count | Terms as far as read |
    23	|---|---|---|---|---|
    24	| United Kingdom | NSTA ArcGIS Online, `UKCS offshore petroleum licence blocks WGS84` FeatureServer/0 (+ England onshore) | licences via `LICREF`; block name `BLOCKREF` | 698 + 193 block rows | "NSTA Open User Licence"; acknowledgement required; the licence PDF returned 404: **not read in full** |
    25	| Norway | Sodir FactMaps `FactMapsWGS84` FeatureServer 616 (production licences), 802 (blocks) | 616; block name from 802 `blcName` | 1,813 / 1,827 | NLOD by Sodir's open-data page (page returned 403 to the reader): **credit wording not verified** |
    26	| United States | BOEM `MMC_Layers` MapServer 15 (leases), 11 (block grid, 278,438); BLM MLRS leases FeatureServer/0 (466,838 cases) | BOEM leases first; BLM is its own slice | 1,875 | BOEM: no licence text on the service; BLM: "should be cited as the data source" |
    27	
    28	**The design the charter fixes.**
    29	
    30	1. *Terms first (slice 0, records class, no code).* For NSTA, Sodir, BOEM and BLM: open the
    31	   licence text itself (not a search summary), quote the sentences that allow re-use and
    32	   redistribution of derived tiles and the required credit line, with the address and the date, in
    33	   `areas/SOURCES.md` under "Licences" and in `docs/program/evidence/e51/terms.md`. A human-check
    34	   line per source as for records. Where the text cannot be opened from the controller, the lane
    35	   says how it tried and adds an owner-actions item to open it in a browser; that country waits,
    36	   the others proceed (R-S5).
    37	2. *A regulator is a source with a reader, not a file by hand.* `areas/licence/<cc>.yaml` names
    38	   the service, the layer, the id and name attributes, the block-name attribute or the block layer
    39	   to join, the filter for "current", the licence and credit; `osd areas read <cc>` fetches it
    40	   with the verifier's readers and writes `areas/licence/<cc>.geojson` (area/1, `kind: licence`,
    41	   `source.retrieved` = the read time, one feature per licence: the block rows of one `LICREF`
    42	   dissolved to a multipolygon, `blocks` = the sorted block names). Network: AGENTS.md's network
    43	   line gains "`osd areas read`, which reads the named regulators' public licence layers, run by
    44	   the `areas` workflow or a maintainer". Tests inject the fetcher.
    45	3. *The schedule (an exception to R6, by owner decision OSD-D29).* A workflow `areas.yml`: weekly
    46	   cron and dispatch; runs `osd areas read` per country; opens (or updates) one pull request
    47	   "Licences read <date>" when a file changed, with the count before and after per country; `check`
    48	   gates it like any change; the supervisor merges. It never pushes to main. A failed or empty
    49	   read, or a count that falls by more than a fifth, changes nothing and comments on the standing
    50	   issue for that country: the last good copy stays, with its date.
    51	4. *The count and the row.* E46's rule, unchanged, with `kind: licence`: only licences holding a
    52	   position are written to `areas.json` and the tiles. `records[].areas.licence` lists them; the
    53	   build also writes, per record with at most 25 such licences, `blocks`: the block names of the
    54	   licences its positions are in (the dataset row shows "Blocks 15/9, 15/12 …"; a national
    55	   register with thousands shows the count). `areas.json` carries `retrieved` per country.
    56	5. *The surface, small, at the end of each country slice.* E48's switch shows Licences when the
    57	   kind exists; the attribution shows "Licences: NSTA, read 24 Nov 2026" from `areas.json`; the
    58	   row shows the blocks. J13 is lit with the first country.
    59	6. *Slices.* 0 terms (opens at once). 1 United Kingdom with the contract (`areas read`, the
    60	   workflow, the count for licences). 2 Norway. 3 United States: BOEM leases; BLM only if its
    61	   466,838 cases reduce to current leases holding a dataset inside the size budget, else a
    62	   finding. Each country is one PR.
    63	
    64	**Acceptance.**
    65	
    66	1. Slice 0: `terms.md` holds, per source, the quoted sentences, the address, the date and the
    67	   credit line, or the sentence "not opened: <how tried>" with the owner item number. No country's
    68	   geometry is committed before its terms line exists (test: `osd validate` refuses a licence area
    69	   file whose `source.licence` or `source.credit` is empty: E46 guard reused).
    70	2. Slice 1: `osd areas read gb` against a recorded fixture response writes the golden
    71	   `gb.geojson`: one feature per licence, block rows dissolved, `blocks` sorted; pagination past
    72	   `maxRecordCount` is exercised by the fixture.
    73	3. A fixture read with zero features, an HTTP error, or a count 30 % lower leaves the committed
    74	   file byte-identical and exits with the finding (three tests; mutation: the guard removed
    75	   replaces the file).
    76	4. Fixture build: a well in licence P1 and none in P2 gives P1 in `areas.json` and not P2;
    77	   the record's `blocks` are P1's; a record with 26 licences gets a count, not a list.
    78	5. Real catalogue, per country PR: the number of licences read, the number holding a dataset, the
    79	   datasets that gained `blocks`, and the size added to git and to the tiles.
    80	6. J13: on the fixture build the switch shows Licences, a click on P1 filters the list, the row
    81	   names its block, the attribution names the regulator and the read date. Without licence data
    82	   the fourth part of the switch is absent.
    83	7. `areas.yml` on a dispatched run in the lane's branch (dry: no PR opened) prints the diff
    84	   summary; the workflow file is announced in the PR title.
    85	8. `make check` remains offline and under 120 s; the licence files add under 10 MB to git for the
    86	   three countries together (else the stop rule).
    87	
    88	**Out of scope.** Grid blocks as drawn areas; unlicensed or relinquished acreage; Canada,
    89	Australia, the Netherlands, Brazil, New Zealand, Denmark, Germany (terms unread: a follow-on
    90	charter per the owner's order); EMODnet's European compilation (yearly, behind the regulators: not
    91	used where a regulator is read).
    92	
    93	**Stop rules.** A source whose terms forbid redistribution of derived data, or stay unread: that
    94	country is not drawn; write the finding and go on with the next. If dissolved licences for one
    95	country exceed 5 MB after simplification, stop with the sizes.
    96	
    97	**Ownership and dependencies.** Slice 0: records lane; paths `docs/program/evidence/e51/**` and
    98	the "Licences" section of `areas/SOURCES.md` (handed to the supervisor as a file in the evidence
    99	folder while E46 holds `areas/**`). Slices 1–3: coding lane (kernel) after E46 slice 1 and E48
   100	have merged; paths `areas/licence/**`, `src/osd/areas.py` (the reader and the `blocks` rule),
   101	`src/osd/cli.py` (`areas read`), `src/osd/build.py` (licence layer), `.github/workflows/areas.yml`
   102	(new, announced), `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` (network sentence), `tests/test_areas_read.py`,
   103	`tests/fixtures/areas/licence/**`, `site/shop.js`, `tests/site/shop.test.mjs` (the row's blocks
   104	line, the read date, J13).
